{
    "name": "The Latin Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Latin people, heirs to a culture that transformed a modest city beside the Tiber into the dominant power of central Italy. Discipline, law, and stubborn determination have carried Rome further than many believed possible. The Senate calls it virtue. Their enemies usually call it invasion.\n\nYet Italia remains divided. Celtic tribes hold the north, Greek cities flourish in the south, and proud peoples across the peninsula have little interest in being told they are now part of someone else's glorious future.\n\nRome has won many battles, but conquest is easier than unity. Roads must be built, allies rewarded, rebels discouraged, and taxes collected from people who somehow never seem grateful.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Italia].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "Pro Roma et Italia!!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Latin Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
