},
{
    "name": "The Celtic Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Celtic peoples, heirs to a culture that stretches from the Atlantic Ocean to the mountains of Anatolia. Though divided into countless tribes and kingdoms, the Celts share a legacy of fearless warriors, master craftsmen, and storytellers who preserve history without needing to carve every argument into stone.\n\nYet unity has never been a Celtic specialty. Every chieftain believes they deserve to lead, every tribe treasures its independence, and settling disputes by charging at one another has somehow remained a popular form of diplomacy.\n\nPowerful neighbors gather beyond your frontiers. Rome marches steadily north, Carthage seeks new allies, and Hellenistic kings cast long shadows across the east. Whether the Celtic world rises together or falls apart one glorious tribal feud at a time depends entirely upon you.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Gallia].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "For the Tribes!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Celtic Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
            ]
        }
    ],
    "civilopediaText": [
