            "text": "Review the Civilopedia -> Building -> Gallia",
            "link": "Buildings/Gallia"
        },
        {
            "text": "VICTORY CONDITIONS",
            "link": "Resources/Celtic Grand Campaign"
        }
    ]
},
{
    "name": "The Germanic Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Germanic peoples, heirs to a culture forged in vast forests, winding rivers, and untamed frontiers. Though divided into countless tribes, they are bound by fierce independence, loyalty to kin, and warriors whose courage is measured not by polished armor, but by the willingness to stand beside their shield-wall.\n\nNo single king rules Germania. Every chieftain guards the freedom of his own people, every tribe values its customs above another's, and convincing them to cooperate is often harder than defeating a foreign army. Fortunately, outsiders have always been remarkably effective at reminding the tribes they have something in common.\n\nBeyond the forests, ambitious civilizations grow ever stronger. Celtic kingdoms dominate the west, Roman influence creeps northward, and wealthy merchants seek to turn your rivers into their roads. Whether Germania remains a land of scattered tribes or rises as a united people rests entirely upon your leadership.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Germania].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "For Germania!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Germanic Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
            ]
        }
    ],
    "civilopediaText": [
        {
            "text": "Review the Civilopedia -> Building -> Germania",
            "link": "Buildings/Germania"
        },
        {
            "text": "VICTORY CONDITIONS",
            "link": "Resources/Germanic Grand Campaign"
        }
    ]
},
{
    "name": "The Iberian Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Iberian peoples, heirs to a culture shaped by rugged mountains, fertile valleys, and the seas that connect the western Mediterranean. Though divided among kingdoms, tribes, and prosperous cities, the peoples of Hispania are renowned as skilled warriors, accomplished metalworkers, and merchants whose wealth attracts almost as much attention as their silver.\n\nUnity, however, has never come easily. Every tribe values its independence, every city guards its own interests, and every ambitious neighbor somehow discovers that Iberian silver is essential to their glorious future. It is a remarkable coincidence that has repeated itself for centuries.\n\nTo the north lie proud Celtic tribes, across the sea the great powers of Carthage and Rome compete for influence, and every victory invites another foreign army eager to explain the benefits of liberation. Whether Hispania remains a land divided or rises beneath one banner now rests in your hands.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Hispania].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "¡Por Hispania!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Iberian Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
