            "link": "Resources/Iberian Grand Campaign"
        }
    ]
},
{
    "name": "The Punic Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Punic people, heirs to a civilization born from Phoenician merchants who carried their language, gods, and ambition across the Mediterranean. From humble trading posts grew prosperous cities, and from prosperous cities emerged Carthage, whose wealth now rivals the greatest powers of the ancient world.\n\nThe Punic way is built upon commerce, seamanship, and opportunity. Every harbor is a gateway to fortune, every colony a new market, and every successful voyage somehow encourages another tax collector to appear. Trade, it seems, has always been a team effort.\n\nYet prosperity invites envy. Rome eyes the western seas with growing confidence, ambitious kings seek control of your trade routes, and distant colonies demand both protection and profit. The Mediterranean has become a battlefield where fleets often decide what armies merely confirm.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Africa Pacata].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "For Carthage and Baal Hammon!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Punic Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
