{
    "name": "The Numidian Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Numidian people, heirs to a culture shaped by the open plains, rugged mountains, and endless horizons of North Africa. Though divided among rival kingdoms and proud tribes, the Numidians are renowned as unmatched horsemen, skilled hunters, and warriors whose speed has frustrated armies far larger than their own.\n\nThe Numidian way values freedom above all else. Every chieftain guards the independence of his people, every rider answers first to their own clan, and persuading them to follow one banner often requires as much diplomacy as courage. Horses, fortunately, have always been easier to convince than politicians.\n\nTo the east, Carthage seeks loyal allies. Across the sea, Rome grows ever more ambitious. Both powers covet Numidian cavalry, though neither seems particularly interested in asking politely. Whether your people remain divided between foreign empires or forge a kingdom worthy of their ancestors now rests in your hands.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Africa Pacata].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
