{
    "name": "The Nomadic Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Nomadic peoples, heirs to a culture born upon the endless grasslands stretching from the Danube to the distant east. The open steppe is your homeland, the horse your closest companion, and freedom your most treasured possession. Kingdoms rise and fall, but the horizon remains unchanged.\n\nThe Nomadic way is one of movement rather than walls. Tribes gather beneath great chieftains when necessity demands, then drift apart once victory has been won. Every clan values its independence, every rider seeks glory, and every settled kingdom eventually discovers that defending a frontier several thousand miles long is remarkably inconvenient.\n\nGreat empires surround the steppe. Greek merchants seek your horses, Persian kings demand your allegiance, and ambitious rulers dream of taming lands that have humbled conquerors for centuries. They often learn that maps are considerably easier to command than horse archers.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Pontus Euxinus].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
