{
    "name": "The Hellenistic Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Hellenistic peoples, heirs to the empire forged by Alexander the Great. Though his empire shattered soon after his death, its legacy endured in mighty kingdoms where Greek language, philosophy, and institutions blended with the ancient traditions of Egypt, Persia, Anatolia, and beyond. The empire itself vanished. The idea proved considerably more difficult to kill.\n\nThe Hellenistic world thrives upon ambitious kings, prosperous cities, and scholars whose debates are nearly as fierce as the wars between their patrons. Every ruler claims to be Alexander's rightful successor, despite the minor inconvenience that Alexander never appointed one. History has been arguing over the matter ever since.\n\nYet the Successor Kingdoms remain divided. Rival dynasties wage endless wars for supremacy, Rome begins casting its gaze eastward, and ambitious barbarians probe the frontiers. Whether the Hellenistic world remains fractured or rises beneath one banner now rests in your hands.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Anatolia].",
    "presentation": "Alert",
    "choices": [
        {
            "text": "For Alexander's Legacy!",
            "uniques": [
                "Instantly provides [1] [Hellenistic Grand Campaign] <hidden from users>",
