{
    "name": "The Illyrian Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Illyrian people, heirs to a culture forged among the rugged mountains and indented coastlines of the western Balkans. Though divided into kingdoms and tribal confederations, the Illyrians are renowned as fierce warriors, skilled sailors, and hardy highlanders who have never found surrender to be a particularly attractive custom.\n\nThe Illyrian way values freedom, clan, and opportunity. Some tribes prosper through trade across the Adriatic, others through mining the mountains, and a few have discovered that collecting cargo from passing ships without asking permission can be remarkably profitable. Their neighbors, curiously, insist on calling this piracy.\n\nYet Illyricum remains fractured. Rival chiefs compete for influence, Macedonia seeks dominance beyond the mountains, and the Roman Republic has begun taking an unhealthy interest in the Adriatic. History suggests that whenever Rome becomes interested in a coastline, someone else's independence is about to become negotiable.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Illyricum].",
