{
    "name": "The Thracian Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Thracian people, heirs to a culture that flourished between the Danube, the Carpathian Mountains, and the Aegean Sea. Though divided into many tribes and kingdoms, the Thracians share a reputation as formidable warriors, accomplished horsemen, and skilled craftsmen whose treasures have filled both royal tombs and the ambitions of foreign conquerors.\n\nThe Thracian spirit values courage and independence above all else. Every king dreams of ruling the neighboring tribes, every chieftain believes their people deserve freedom, and every generation somehow discovers that settling old rivalries with sharp weapons only creates exciting new rivalries.\n\nPowerful neighbors surround your homeland. Macedonian kings seek influence in the south, Celtic tribes wander across the north, and Rome steadily expands toward the Balkans. They all covet the wealth and strategic lands of Thrace. Whether your people remain divided or rise beneath a single banner now rests in your hands.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Dacia Maior].",
