{
    "name": "The Eastern Awakening",
    "text": "247 BC\n\nYou lead the Eastern peoples, heirs to the ancient civilizations that flourished between the Tigris and Euphrates. Here, the first great cities rose from the floodplains, kings carved their triumphs into stone, and scribes recorded history long before many nations had decided that writing was worth the effort.\n\nEmpires have come and gone across Mesopotamia. Sumerians, Assyrians, Babylonians, Persians, and Macedonians have each claimed dominion over these fertile lands, only to discover that ruling the cradle of civilization is considerably easier than keeping it. Every conqueror believes they have built an eternal empire. Archaeology politely disagrees.\n\nYet the cities endure. Babylon still commands respect, merchants carry wealth along ancient rivers, and ambitious rulers continue to compete for the richest lands in the Near East. Whether the East remains divided between rival kingdoms or rises beneath a single banner now rests in your hands.\n\nYour first objective is clear.\n\nUnite [Mesopotamia Maior].",
